<%# Long laws keep their complete contents in the main column as well as the
    searchable sidebar, open as on any other law (until 2026-10-16 it started
    closed, and readers took the card for a pointer to the sidebar). The list
    scrolls inside a bounded region, so WER's 1,639 entries cannot bury the
    text again; the native details still folds it, with or without scripts.
    Print expands the full list through the scoped law-main-toc-disclosure
    rules. Nothing stands below the list: the heading gives the count and the
    sidebar has its own controls (a note and two shortcut buttons were removed
    at the owner's request on 2026-11-02). %>
<div class="p-4 md:p-6" data-toc-summary>
  <details class="law-main-toc-disclosure" data-main-toc-disclosure open>
    <summary class="w-full min-h-11 flex items-center justify-between gap-2 cursor-pointer text-left focus:outline-hidden focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-(--accent-500) group transition-colors">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-(--accent-500) group-hover:text-(--accent-600) transition-colors"><%= t(:toc).capitalize %> <span class="text-base font-normal text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">(<%= count %>)</span></h2>
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 law-main-toc-chevron print:hidden" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 10.94l3.71-3.71a.75.75 0 111.06 1.06l-4.24 4.24a.75.75 0 01-1.06 0L5.21 8.29a.75.75 0 01.02-1.08z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
      </svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="mt-4" data-main-toc-list>
      <%= render 'toc', content: content, hide_header: true, scrollable: false, track: false, variant: :main %>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
